  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sharif Ahmed Shafiq Ahmed Alvi vs The State Of Maharashtra on 5 July, 2022 Author: Bharati Dangre Bench: Bharati Dangre 1/4 26 ABA-1647.22.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.1647 Of 2022 Sharif Ahmed Shafiq Ahmed Alvi ] ... Applicant Vs. The State of Maharashtra ] ... Respondent ... Mr. M. Shah with Mr. Kunal Bilaney i/b Mr. Kushal Mor for the applicant. Ms. A.A. Takalkar, A.P.P. for the State. Mr. Rahul Rakh, Pi attached to Crime Branch is present. ... Coram : Smt. Bharati Dangre, J. Dated : 05Th July, 2022. P.C.:- 1. 2. The applicant is apprehending his arrest in C.R.No. 183 of 2022 registered with Mira Road Police Station invoking Sections AJN 2/4 26 ABA-1647.22.odt",
    "facts": "2. The applicant is apprehending his arrest in C.R.No. 183 of 2022 registered with Mira Road Police Station invoking Sections AJN 2/4 26 ABA-1647.22.odt 3. On 27/4/2022, on a secret information being received to the effect that the prohibited substance in the form of Gutka, Paan Masala, Scented Tobacco, and Mixture of Betel nut were being transported, a raid was conducted and some white bags were recovered from the back seat of the rickshaw. The said bags contained the prohibited substance and the rickshaw driver as well as the persons accompanying him were brought to the police station. The prohibited substance was found to be worth Rs.37,800/- (SHK Gutka) Rs.23,700/- (Vimal Gutka) and Tobacco worth Rs.2,640/-. During investigation, the name of the applicant was surfaced as dealer of the prohibited substance. That is how, he is named as accused in the C.R. 4. Barring the offence under Section 328 of the IPC, all other offences are bailable. The position of law whether an offence under Section 328 of the IPC gets attracted when the prohibited substance, is transported or supplied is not yet crystallized. The special leave petition is directed to be tagged with the special leave petition filed by the State of Maharashtra in case of Anand Chaurasiya (supra).",
    "arguments": "A decision of the Division Bench of this Court in case of Anand Ramdhani Chaurasiya & Anr. v. The State of Maharashtra [(2019) SCC Online Bombay 1857], where a view was taken that Section 328 of the IPC could not have been invoked, has been stayed by the Hon'ble Apex Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "A decision of the Division Bench of this Court in case of Anand Ramdhani Chaurasiya & Anr. v. The State of Maharashtra [(2019) SCC Online Bombay 1857], where a view was taken that Section 328 of the IPC could not have been invoked, has been stayed by the Hon'ble Apex Court."
  },
